# Scratch planning

If this effort has a `map.md`, you are **wayfinding**: resolve one decision
ticket, do not implement product code unless that map's Notes explicitly carry
execution.

- Decision tickets: `Type: research|prototype|grilling|task` and
  `Status: open|claimed|resolved`. Claim before work. One grilling ticket per
  session. Sub-agents may resolve research; they must not answer grilling.
  HITL grilling rounds use Cursor **AskQuestion** (option picker; recommended
  choice first, labeled `(Recommended)`), not markdown-only ❓ blocks.
- Never add `Status: ready-for-agent` (implementation) tickets next to a map.
  After the map is clear, create a **new** `.scratch/<feature>/` with `spec.md`.
- Chat memory of this map is stale after compression. Re-read `map.md` and the
  claimed ticket from disk before grilling, answering, or resolving. Do not
  trust a summary of Decisions-so-far.
- If this effort has a `loop.md`, you are in a **conductor** loop: chat memory
  of the goal and predicate is stale after compression. First tool call every
  turn (including `/loop` wakes) is
  `NeuralAmpModeler/scripts/conductor-status.ps1 -Effort <slug>`. Do not trust
  a summary of Goal, Predicate, Verifier, or Ledger. Append ledger rows; never
  rewrite them from memory. Mechanics: `.cursor/skills/conductor/SKILL.md`.
- Ops: `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`. Do not publish maps to GitHub Issues.
